Feature: Channel-wise Sales Performance Analysis for Biosimilar Brands

  This feature calculates the total sales performance of biosimilar products (Kanjinti, Mvasi, Riabni) across different channels (online, retail, mobile) by aggregating sales metrics within a 36-month window from cdl_effective_date, grouped by key attributes.

  Background:
    Given the source table "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack" exists in Unity Catalog "purgo_databricks" schema "purgo_playground"
    And the columns brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name, transaction_timestamp, integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, integrated_dollars, cdl_effective_date are present
    And the biosimilar brands to include are "Kanjinti", "Mvasi", "Riabni" in brand_normalized_name
    And the valid channels are "online", "retail", "mobile"
    And cdl_effective_date is in string format "yyyy-MM-dd"
    And the 36-month window is calculated as records where transaction_timestamp >= date_add(cdl_effective_date, 0) and transaction_timestamp < date_add(cdl_effective_date, 36 months)
    And records with null or invalid cdl_effective_date are excluded and logged to "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_invalid_cdl_effective_date_log" with error_message "Invalid or null cdl_effective_date"
    And all values of competitor_flag (true/false) are included
    And duplicate records are removed based on all grouping keys and transaction_timestamp

  Scenario: Aggregate sales metrics for biosimilar brands by channel within 36 months of cdl_effective_date
    Given the dataset is filtered for brand_normalized_name in ["Kanjinti", "Mvasi", "Riabni"]
    And channel_name in ["online", "retail", "mobile"]
    And cdl_effective_date is not null and matches format "yyyy-MM-dd"
    And transaction_timestamp is within 36 months from cdl_effective_date
    When the data is grouped by brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name
    Then the output contains sum of integrated_units as total_integrated_units
    And sum of integrated_normalized_units as total_integrated_normalized_units
    And sum of integrated_dollars as total_integrated_dollars
    And the result is written to "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_channelwise_stg" with columns:
      | brand_normalized_name | normalized_name | market_normalized_name | competitor_flag | channel_name | total_integrated_units | total_integrated_normalized_units | total_integrated_dollars |

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for invalid or null cdl_effective_date
    Given a record with brand_normalized_name "<brand>"
    And cdl_effective_date "<cdl_effective_date>"
    When cdl_effective_date is null or does not match format "yyyy-MM-dd"
    Then the record is excluded from aggregation
    And the record is logged to "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_invalid_cdl_effective_date_log" with error_message "Invalid or null cdl_effective_date"

    Examples:
      | brand     | cdl_effective_date |
      | Kanjinti  | null              |
      | Mvasi     | 2022-13-01        |
      | Riabni    | 2021/05/01        |

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven aggregation for biosimilar brands and channels
    Given brand_normalized_name "<brand>"
    And channel_name "<channel>"
    And cdl_effective_date "<cdl_effective_date>"
    And transaction_timestamp "<transaction_timestamp>"
    And integrated_units <units>
    And integrated_normalized_units <normalized_units>
    And integrated_dollars <dollars>
    When transaction_timestamp is within 36 months from cdl_effective_date
    Then the record is included in aggregation
    And the aggregated totals are calculated per group

    Examples:
      | brand     | channel | cdl_effective_date | transaction_timestamp | units | normalized_units | dollars |
      | Kanjinti  | online  | 2021-01-01         | 2022-01-01           | 100   | 90               | 10000   |
      | Mvasi     | retail  | 2020-06-15         | 2021-06-15           | 200   | 180              | 20000   |
      | Riabni    | mobile  | 2019-12-01         | 2020-12-01           | 150   | 140              | 15000   |

  Scenario: Exclude records outside the 36-month window
    Given a record with cdl_effective_date "2020-01-01"
    And transaction_timestamp "2024-02-01"
    When transaction_timestamp is not within 36 months from cdl_effective_date
    Then the record is excluded from aggregation

  Scenario: Include all competitor_flag values
    Given records with competitor_flag true and false
    When aggregating sales metrics
    Then both true and false competitor_flag records are included in the output

  Scenario: Remove duplicate records
    Given duplicate records with same brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name, transaction_timestamp
    When aggregating sales metrics
    Then only one record per unique combination is included in the aggregation

  Scenario: Output format validation
    Given the aggregation is complete
    When writing to "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_channelwise_stg"
    Then the output table contains columns:
      | brand_normalized_name | normalized_name | market_normalized_name | competitor_flag | channel_name | total_integrated_units | total_integrated_normalized_units | total_integrated_dollars |
    And all values are non-null except where source data is null

  Scenario: Channel filter validation
    Given channel_name is in ["online", "retail", "mobile"]
    When aggregating sales metrics
    Then only records with channel_name in the specified list are included

  Scenario: Aggregation metric validation
    Given integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, integrated_dollars are present
    When aggregating
    Then sum of each metric is calculated per group
    And no other metrics are included in the output

  Scenario: Data integrity for null sales metrics
    Given a record with null integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, or integrated_dollars
    When aggregating
    Then null values are treated as zero in the sum

  Scenario: Output destination validation
    Given the aggregation is complete
    When writing results
    Then the output is written to "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_channelwise_stg"
    And the output format matches the table definition

